face-image: img/luigi_is_good.jpeg

= Sturzo Dismissed!

Luigi Sturzo, head of the PPI, and notable collaborator with us, has had a meeting with Pope Pius XI. It is likely that the Vatican has secured a deal with the <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">fascists</span> and [+ prime_minister +], in exchange for solving the Roman Question.

Beforehand, he had been pressured by his party to resign, with several figures siding agaisnt him, notably Meda, on the electoral reform, with Sturzo being a fierce opponent of <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">fascist</span> dictatorship. The party's right has given Sturzo an ultimatum.

<div style="text-align: center; margin: 1em 0px; display: block;">
> *“The Vatican will not always be able to remain impassive before the open struggle going on between the <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">Fascisti</span> and the <span style="color: [+ ppi_colour +];">partisans of Don Sturzo</span> Until the present moment the latter has been protected by Cardinal Gasparri (the Papal Secretary of State) but the time has come when it is no longer possible for the Secretary of State to be identified with him. If Don Sturzo does not retire a schism in the <span style="color: [+ ppi_colour +];">Popular Party</span> is certain.”*

- @root: Sturzo resigns, and <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> continues its slippery-slope into dictatorship.
